# TES Repository Map

## Purpose

This page is the source-oriented map for the TES repository. It complements [[TES Spring Boot Modules]] with the current Gradle module list and the non-module roots that affect runtime, configuration, deployment, and documentation.

Authoritative build sources:

- `settings.gradle`
- `build.gradle`
- `gradle/`
- `gradle.properties`

## Gradle modules

| Module | Role evidenced by source/build |
|---|---|
| `tes-coreapi` | Shared Java/Kotlin contracts: commands, events, IDs, task/work models, workflow definitions, application types, DTOs, integration contracts |
| `tes-common` | Shared view/query models and common utilities |
| `tes-config` | Configuration loading and config-domain support |
| `tes-host-importer` | Host/inbound integration |
| `tes-host-exporter` | Host/outbound integration |
| `tes-message-broker` | RabbitMQ/message-broker integration |
| `tes-engine` | Axon aggregates, command/event orchestration, workflow engine, task dispatch, projections/query context, persistence-facing domain services |
| `tes-app` | Published TES application/server container |
| `tes-agent` | Local agent container: REST/websocket application controllers, equipment/resource adapters, manufacturer integrations |
| `tes-test` | Cross-module tests and test support |
| `tes-webui-api` | Web UI/API-facing contracts and endpoints |
| `tes-inventory` | Inventory-specific domain/query functionality |
| `tes-activity` | Activity implementations: picking, putaway, count, receiving, shipping, move, G2P, production, and application state machines |
| `tes-simulator` | Simulation runtime and simulated device/application behavior |

The included modules are declared in `settings.gradle`. The two published container projects are `tes-app` and `tes-agent`; `tes-coreapi` is also published as a library according to `build.gradle`.

## Runtime boundaries

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    Core[tes-coreapi] --> Engine[tes-engine]
    Core --> Activity[tes-activity]
    Core --> Agent[tes-agent]
    Engine --> App[tes-app]
    Engine --> Agent
    Activity --> Engine
    Agent --> Broker[tes-message-broker]
    Engine --> Broker
    Import[tes-host-importer] --> Engine
    Engine --> Export[tes-host-exporter]
    UI[tes-webui-api] --> App
    Sim[tes-simulator] -. simulated runtime .-> Agent
```

This is a dependency/runtime boundary diagram, not a complete Gradle dependency graph. Verify exact dependencies in each module's `build.gradle`.

## Important source roots

- Domain contracts: `tes-coreapi/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/`
- Shared query/view models: `tes-common/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/common/`
- Workflow/activity implementations: `tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/`
- Engine orchestration: `tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/`
- Agent REST/websocket and equipment integrations: `tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/`
- Configuration: `tes-config/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/config/` and `resources/config/`
- Host integration: `tes-host-importer/src/main/java/`, `tes-host-exporter/src/main/java/`
- Broker integration: `tes-message-broker/src/main/java/`
- HTTP/API contract: `tes-webui-api/src/main/java/`, `api-docs.json`
- Deployment/build support: `config/`, `.github/`, `Dockerfile*`, `build.gradle`

