## Build and packaging facts

From `build.gradle`:

- Java and Kotlin toolchains target Java 21.
- Spring Boot, Spring AMQP, Axon, Spring Cloud Consul, Spring Web, JPA, Security, websocket, and actuator dependencies are applied broadly to subprojects.
- `tes-app` and `tes-agent` produce published WAR/container artifacts.
- Most non-container modules disable `bootJar`; `tes-coreapi` and other libraries publish Java components.
- Boot build-image configuration is applied to the published container projects.
- OpenAPI generation uses `api-docs.json` and writes to `tes-openapi-client`.

## Scope boundary

This map describes the repository topology and build declarations. For detailed runtime behavior, follow [[TES Architecture]], [[TES Bounded Contexts]], [[TES Runtime Flows]], [[TES RabbitMQ Topology]], and [[TES Deployment Architecture]].
